      ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x y^{2}-4 x^{5} y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x y^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{5} y) \\\\  & =2 y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x)-4 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{5}) \\\\  & =2 y^{2}\\cdot (1)-4 y\\cdot (5 x^{4}) \\\\  & =2 y^{2}-20 x^{4} y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(1,2)} & =2 (2)^{2}-20 (1)^{4} (2) \\\\  & =8-(40) \\\\  & =-32\\end{aligned}\n$$",
